<h2>Container queries</h2>

<p>The <code>.media</code> component uses a container query to switch from stacked to side-by-side layout based on its own available width, not the viewport. This makes it safe to place in any column width without breakpoint overrides.</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Container queries let components own their responsive behaviour. The parent decides how much space to give; the component decides what to do with it.</p>
</blockquote>

<h2>Fluid spacing and type</h2>

<p>Every spacing and type token is <code>clamp()</code>-based. This eliminates most breakpoint-specific overrides: the scale compresses gracefully on small screens and expands on large ones. The only breakpoints left are structural — the nav collapse and the two-column media layout.</p>

<p>The result is a site that feels intentional at every width without a wall of media queries.</p>
